1
00:02:30,035 --> 00:02:36,725
Please contact us for any inquiries
turkision@gmail.com

2
00:02:51,612 --> 00:02:54,452
When will the raft come to
take us, Andreas?

3
00:02:54,821 --> 00:02:59,861
According to Lord Rogatos' messenger,
they should have come already, sir Grego.

4
00:03:07,993 --> 00:03:09,563
Soldiers!

5
00:03:09,733 --> 00:03:14,480
We'll take Father Gregor and return to the
castle with the order of Lord Rogatos!

6
00:03:14,480 --> 00:03:16,250
I don't want any trouble!

7
00:03:18,695 --> 00:03:20,235
My Alps!

8
00:03:21,097 --> 00:03:24,637
With Allah's permission,
we are going to...

9
00:03:25,594 --> 00:03:29,104
fly like an eagle,
take Father Gregor and...

10
00:03:29,104 --> 00:03:31,886
return to our land.

11
00:03:31,886 --> 00:03:34,286
- Inshallah my Bey.
- Inshallah my Bey.

12
00:03:40,235 --> 00:03:42,765
There, there he is, sir

13
00:04:30,706 --> 00:04:32,236
Father Gregor.

14
00:04:33,879 --> 00:04:37,869
Bilecik's Lord Rogatus sent me
to take you.

15
00:04:38,312 --> 00:04:40,452
Nice, nice.

16
00:04:41,545 --> 00:04:43,495
My friend Rogatus.

17
00:04:43,572 --> 00:04:46,552
Lord Rogatus' loyal soldiers are waiting
for you.

18
00:04:48,178 --> 00:04:49,478
Here.

19
00:04:49,549 --> 00:04:50,889
Here.

20
00:04:52,026 --> 00:04:53,136
Come.

21
00:04:58,753 --> 00:05:00,903
God bless you, son.

22
00:05:04,701 --> 00:05:05,701
Here.

23
00:05:09,349 --> 00:05:11,469
Come, here.

24
00:05:16,910 --> 00:05:18,210
Here.

25
00:06:09,834 --> 00:06:11,684
We'll wait here.

26
00:06:12,782 --> 00:06:15,602
Let's see when they'll fall into
our clutches.

27
00:06:20,906 --> 00:06:22,746
- Baysungur.
- My Bey.

28
00:06:23,024 --> 00:06:25,154
You know what to do.

29
00:06:26,075 --> 00:06:27,535
I know, my Bey.

30
00:06:28,493 --> 00:06:30,083
Go.

31
00:07:38,654 --> 00:07:40,504
My dear friend.

32
00:07:41,085 --> 00:07:42,761
Where are we going?

33
00:07:42,761 --> 00:07:46,230
Where exactly are Feodor and
his loyal soldiers waiting for us?

34
00:07:46,230 --> 00:07:49,110
They are waiting for you Goksu front, sir.

35
00:07:49,488 --> 00:07:50,698
Interesting.

36
00:07:52,468 --> 00:07:55,588
They were supposed to wait for us
around Cakirca.

37
00:07:56,687 --> 00:07:58,747
I think we were mistaken.

38
00:08:26,517 --> 00:08:29,914
Here one of the murderers of his relative,
Michael Kosses...

39
00:08:29,914 --> 00:08:32,664
while we are running away from the Emperor.

40
00:08:35,541 --> 00:08:39,611
Or should I have said
Inegol Lord Aya Nicola?

41
00:08:43,197 --> 00:08:45,187
Search him.

42
00:09:11,024 --> 00:09:12,484
So you are a Turk.

43
00:09:15,531 --> 00:09:17,381
You'll drown.

44
00:09:43,192 --> 00:09:45,482
You'll eat in hell!

45
00:10:37,935 --> 00:10:40,855
The rift is going somewhere else.

46
00:10:41,476 --> 00:10:42,986
Not here.

47
00:10:47,297 --> 00:10:48,917
Cerkutay...

48
00:10:51,519 --> 00:10:53,219
is not on the rift, my Bey.

49
00:10:56,498 --> 00:10:58,148
Let's go!

50
00:11:47,939 --> 00:11:49,769
Catalans!

51
00:12:01,864 --> 00:12:04,124
Deploy!

52
00:12:05,149 --> 00:12:06,659
Do not show mercy!

53
00:12:06,961 --> 00:12:09,581
Bring Father, kill the rest!

54
00:12:11,089 --> 00:12:13,679
Damn it!
Where did they come from?

55
00:12:16,074 --> 00:12:18,594
For the Lasgaris dynasty!

56
00:13:26,003 --> 00:13:28,543
There was supposed to be only Rogatus!

57
00:13:28,581 --> 00:13:31,881
- Is this for the Emperor, sir Gregor?
- I don't know, Andreas!

58
00:15:17,721 --> 00:15:19,391
Father Gregor.

59
00:21:06,482 --> 00:21:08,532
You maniac!

60
00:21:48,144 --> 00:21:50,934
Where is the Father?

61
00:21:51,517 --> 00:21:53,867
Are you asking me, Diego?

62
00:21:54,466 --> 00:21:58,606
You were supposed to get him while
I was fighting, Diego!

63
00:22:04,698 --> 00:22:06,748
Father Gregor...

64
00:22:07,410 --> 00:22:13,140
From now on, you are in hands of Osman Bey,
the son of Kayi Bey Ertugrul Ghazi.

65
00:22:18,887 --> 00:22:20,697
I've heard your name.

66
00:22:22,196 --> 00:22:28,756
All the east churches damned you for what
you've done to the sons of Jesus, Osman Bey.

67
00:22:35,665 --> 00:22:41,765
I'll give you a chance to let you see
the outcome of your prayers.

68
00:22:42,422 --> 00:22:45,813
Kill me if you are going to kill me.
I am not afraid of you.

69
00:22:45,813 --> 00:22:47,852
I am not afraid of dying at all!

70
00:22:47,852 --> 00:22:49,582
That's fine!

71
00:22:50,423 --> 00:22:52,453
Don't worry.

72
00:22:53,291 --> 00:22:55,681
We'll take care of your goods
and your life.

73
00:23:01,224 --> 00:23:02,464
Alps.

74
00:23:04,308 --> 00:23:06,156
Get him in the tent in secret.

75
00:23:06,156 --> 00:23:08,516
- Eyvallah(okay) my Bey.
- Eyvallah(okay) my Bey.

76
00:23:14,129 --> 00:23:15,999
Bilecik Castle.

77
00:23:21,172 --> 00:23:24,642
I want a cloak out of brocade...

78
00:23:24,707 --> 00:23:26,157
Silas.

79
00:23:26,821 --> 00:23:29,201
It must be processed with gold thread.

80
00:23:30,261 --> 00:23:33,381
I don't want a thick frame.
Two-inch-thick is okay.

81
00:23:36,562 --> 00:23:40,282
There will be a griffon drawing on it.
Oh no, no.

82
00:23:40,815 --> 00:23:43,665
Two griffons looking at each other.

83
00:23:44,374 --> 00:23:48,854
What a beautiful description this is!
Don't worry sir.

84
00:23:49,157 --> 00:23:51,697
We are going to make it as you want.

85
00:23:53,828 --> 00:23:55,108
You know, Silas...

86
00:23:56,036 --> 00:24:00,586
I always respected tailoring.

87
00:24:01,511 --> 00:24:03,851
It's a subtle job.

88
00:24:04,217 --> 00:24:05,197
Very subtle.

89
00:24:05,811 --> 00:24:09,301
However, I don't have that ability.

90
00:24:19,249 --> 00:24:20,339
Sir...

91
00:24:21,489 --> 00:24:23,129
Take them off.

92
00:24:24,446 --> 00:24:26,096
Take them off and get out.

93
00:24:32,970 --> 00:24:34,710
Feodor?

94
00:24:37,000 --> 00:24:38,730
What is up with you?

95
00:24:40,651 --> 00:24:45,371
And of course, where is Father Gregor?

96
00:24:48,823 --> 00:24:50,563
I don't know sir.

97
00:24:53,843 --> 00:24:55,403
We couldn't get him.

98
00:24:55,841 --> 00:24:57,551
You couldn't get him?

99
00:24:59,799 --> 00:25:04,559
Where are your soldiers?
I mean, do you have any left, Feodor?

100
00:25:10,514 --> 00:25:12,604
Tell me what happened there!

101
00:25:18,262 --> 00:25:19,682
C-Catalans...

102
00:25:20,463 --> 00:25:23,081
Catalans sir.
Catalans.

103
00:25:23,081 --> 00:25:24,851
Catalans, huh?

104
00:25:25,214 --> 00:25:27,454
God damn dogs!

105
00:25:28,056 --> 00:25:31,665
For whom Catalans abducted Father Gregor?

106
00:25:31,665 --> 00:25:34,385
They were like waiting for this moment
for years.

107
00:25:34,564 --> 00:25:37,851
My soldiers were not young and
inexperienced. We were not afraid.

108
00:25:37,851 --> 00:25:39,819
We were not afraid, but...

109
00:25:39,819 --> 00:25:41,869
Shut up already!

110
00:25:42,005 --> 00:25:45,755
Catalans have one of the most important
man of God...

111
00:25:45,829 --> 00:25:49,469
... my friend and relative Father Gregor...

112
00:25:49,661 --> 00:25:52,501
... and you are still making up a story!

113
00:25:53,699 --> 00:25:55,499
Someone else took Gregor.

114
00:26:08,936 --> 00:26:10,686
Damn it!

115
00:26:14,442 --> 00:26:16,272
There was someone else.

116
00:26:18,786 --> 00:26:20,596
They were from Bithynia.

117
00:26:23,742 --> 00:26:29,648
That snake must have wrested Father Gregor
off while you were busy with Catalans.

118
00:26:29,648 --> 00:26:31,198
Kosses!

119
00:26:35,376 --> 00:26:37,126
If Kosses has...

120
00:26:37,626 --> 00:26:39,126
...Father Gregor...

121
00:26:41,377 --> 00:26:42,747
...Catalans?

122
00:26:46,341 --> 00:26:48,271
Who are they working for?

123
00:26:49,066 --> 00:26:50,676
For the Emperor?

124
00:26:52,918 --> 00:26:56,698
We are going to figure that out from
Kosses in Nicola's invitation.

125
00:26:59,716 --> 00:27:01,466
Harmankaya Castle.

126
00:27:09,267 --> 00:27:12,037
What is happening, Nestor?
What is this hurry about?

127
00:27:14,057 --> 00:27:16,452
Sir, your sister Mari...

128
00:27:17,270 --> 00:27:19,262
departed from Constantine.

129
00:27:19,262 --> 00:27:22,302
Excellent!
That is good news!

130
00:27:24,042 --> 00:27:25,462
Get out.

131
00:27:28,678 --> 00:27:31,868
Nothing about that damned Jhanselno?

132
00:27:32,111 --> 00:27:34,961
Sir, Catalan Anselmo wants to see you.

133
00:28:02,733 --> 00:28:04,073
This smell...

134
00:28:04,889 --> 00:28:07,209
is the smell of losers.

135
00:28:07,926 --> 00:28:09,366
Anselmo.

136
00:28:11,754 --> 00:28:18,244
This smell is the smell of a silly soldier
who couldn't keep his promise!

137
00:28:19,629 --> 00:28:22,209
This smell is the smell of a corpse...

138
00:28:22,630 --> 00:28:24,040
Anselmo.

139
00:28:25,513 --> 00:28:30,223
As you know, a piece good information
brings victory.

140
00:28:30,870 --> 00:28:33,650
You informed us wrongly!

141
00:28:33,745 --> 00:28:38,215
The whole Bithynia was there
to get the Father!

142
00:28:43,027 --> 00:28:44,777
We lost the Father.

143
00:28:48,705 --> 00:28:51,235
"Wrong information"?

144
00:28:55,086 --> 00:28:58,106
"The whole Bithynia was there."

145
00:28:59,164 --> 00:29:01,144
Do not give me that story, Anselmo.

146
00:29:02,763 --> 00:29:08,433
We made an agreement. I promised you gold
in return for Father Gregor.

147
00:29:08,760 --> 00:29:10,680
I paid you half.

148
00:29:11,385 --> 00:29:14,475
If you win, you win.

149
00:29:14,912 --> 00:29:17,832
If you lose, you lose. again.

150
00:29:20,712 --> 00:29:23,562
Anselmo doesn't lose.

151
00:29:23,590 --> 00:29:26,090
I didn't come all the way from Catalonia.

152
00:29:28,602 --> 00:29:32,262
I'll find Gregor and bring him to you.

153
00:29:32,854 --> 00:29:36,924
I'll get what I want in return.

154
00:29:37,387 --> 00:29:39,627
I am a loyal man to my agreement.

155
00:29:40,232 --> 00:29:43,192
Bring me the Father, get your gold.

156
00:29:45,019 --> 00:29:48,159
You don't even know who has the Father.

157
00:29:48,861 --> 00:29:51,001
We should send our men everywhere, sir.

158
00:29:55,743 --> 00:29:57,643
Everywhere?

159
00:30:02,042 --> 00:30:04,293
Very clever.

160
00:30:07,898 --> 00:30:10,134
I'm invited to Nikola's dinner tonight.

161
00:30:10,134 --> 00:30:15,354
Let's see what will we learn from the
eyes of our 'friendly' lords.

162
00:30:15,354 --> 00:30:17,974
Make your preparations, Mestor.

163
00:30:18,397 --> 00:30:22,894
Bring back your mind, soul
and ideas...

164
00:30:22,894 --> 00:30:26,504
that you left there, in Catalonia!

165
00:30:26,504 --> 00:30:30,894
Or else you will return your home
empty-handed.

166
00:30:42,266 --> 00:30:47,356
I don't lose, he says.
Incompetent.

167
00:30:50,569 --> 00:30:54,229
Thank you, ladies.

168
00:30:56,301 --> 00:31:01,391
Inshallah he'll have a long life
to grow a beard as white as flour.

169
00:31:01,391 --> 00:31:03,481
Amin.

170
00:31:06,166 --> 00:31:10,166
Inshallah he'll have a tongue as
sweet as honey.

171
00:31:10,985 --> 00:31:16,535
Wheat is prosperity, may his
prosperity never end.

172
00:31:19,896 --> 00:31:24,586
Inshallah, his life will be as
clean as salt.

173
00:31:30,367 --> 00:31:35,047
Thank you, Selcan Mother. You doubled
our happiness with your arrival.

174
00:31:35,047 --> 00:31:37,167
Thank you, daughter.

175
00:31:37,167 --> 00:31:41,637
Malhun Hatun is right, mother.
You livened up the tribe.

176
00:31:41,637 --> 00:31:45,457
My pretty girl.
Longing is difficult.

177
00:31:45,457 --> 00:31:47,757
I missed all of you.

178
00:31:49,211 --> 00:31:53,211
Come, ladies. Come.

179
00:31:54,509 --> 00:31:58,509
-Thank you.
-Enjoy it.

180
00:32:03,309 --> 00:32:06,219
Bala?

181
00:32:06,410 --> 00:32:08,620
Are you alright?

182
00:32:13,048 --> 00:32:17,188
I'm fine. I'm fine. I just
got a weird smell.

183
00:32:23,802 --> 00:32:27,802
-Here, Bala.
-Thank you.

184
00:32:30,100 --> 00:32:35,330
May Allah destine you with a long
and glorious life.

185
00:32:35,712 --> 00:32:40,192
May you have a good family.

186
00:32:41,614 --> 00:32:45,614
May Allah protect you from
the evil.

187
00:32:45,614 --> 00:32:49,614
May you be destined to be a worthy
child of your ancestors.

188
00:32:50,473 --> 00:32:54,473
Your Selcan Mother loves you.

189
00:32:54,763 --> 00:32:58,353
My pretty child.

190
00:33:03,129 --> 00:33:08,299
Bala Hatun, you don't look well.
I brought you thymus juice.

191
00:33:11,256 --> 00:33:14,956
What's wrong, my girl?

192
00:33:14,956 --> 00:33:17,826
I'm fine, mother.
I'm fine.

193
00:33:19,157 --> 00:33:23,157
-Here, Malhun.
-Thank you, Gökçe.

194
00:33:24,578 --> 00:33:27,508
Bala!

195
00:33:28,718 --> 00:33:32,718
Come, let's take a walk.
It'll do you good.

196
00:33:32,911 --> 00:33:36,911
-If you allow us.
-Of course, my daughter.

197
00:33:36,911 --> 00:33:39,191
If you allow us.

198
00:33:41,161 --> 00:33:45,161
Ayşe, my girl.
Draw it over.

199
00:33:55,160 --> 00:33:58,600
Who is this girl?
I haven't seen her before.

200
00:33:58,600 --> 00:34:01,610
It's Gökçe.

201
00:34:01,610 --> 00:34:05,610
Ever since Alaca married and left,
she accompanies me.

202
00:34:05,610 --> 00:34:09,610
Good, then. She is skillful.
It shows.

203
00:34:13,039 --> 00:34:16,569
Bala, what are you doing?

204
00:34:16,569 --> 00:34:21,059
You can't drink thymus juice
when you are pregnant.

205
00:34:22,127 --> 00:34:26,127
I don't know, Gonca.
I forgot about it.

206
00:34:26,127 --> 00:34:30,127
Come on, Bala. Please.
Be careful.

207
00:34:30,745 --> 00:34:35,074
What about now?
Are you feeling better?

208
00:34:39,714 --> 00:34:43,873
I'm fine.
I'm fine, Gonca.

209
00:34:43,873 --> 00:34:49,554
Be fine, Bala. Be fine.
But be careful.

210
00:34:53,286 --> 00:34:57,287
Now you carry two lives.

211
00:35:00,135 --> 00:35:03,475
Come.

212
00:35:13,780 --> 00:35:17,780
You are in a great struggle.

213
00:35:17,780 --> 00:35:21,780
I say that this is your biggest
hunt so far.

214
00:35:21,977 --> 00:35:26,417
Catholic and Orthodox fires can
drop on Söğüt any time.

215
00:35:27,348 --> 00:35:31,798
Are we strong enough to
bear this struggle?

216
00:35:31,852 --> 00:35:36,352
In the lands of Anatolia, Turks are
shattered into a thousand pieces.

217
00:35:36,390 --> 00:35:41,160
The Islamic world is fighting over
Shiism and Sunnism.

218
00:35:42,149 --> 00:35:46,659
For this reason, if we are
divided...

219
00:35:46,659 --> 00:35:50,659
they can't be united either.

220
00:35:50,745 --> 00:35:55,055
They will divide too.
They won't unite.

221
00:35:55,055 --> 00:35:59,055
They won't dream about us.

222
00:35:59,939 --> 00:36:04,099
They will have sleepless nights.

223
00:36:05,249 --> 00:36:09,249
They will pay the price...

224
00:36:09,249 --> 00:36:12,329
for every innocent Muslim they killed.

225
00:36:12,829 --> 00:36:16,829
Let them run after us now...

226
00:36:16,829 --> 00:36:20,829
let them try to find a way out now.

227
00:36:23,224 --> 00:36:28,744
My sheik, I'll gain Father Gregor's
trust first.

228
00:36:30,438 --> 00:36:35,108
He and the whole Orthodox people
will see that the Pope isn't the savior.

229
00:36:35,108 --> 00:36:40,178
It's Ottomans who fly
the flag of justice.

230
00:36:40,178 --> 00:36:43,648
Mashallah.
Mashallah.

231
00:36:43,648 --> 00:36:48,508
May your sword be sharp,
your heart be brave.

232
00:36:51,250 --> 00:36:55,650
As long as your heart
is devoted to this...

233
00:36:55,650 --> 00:37:00,300
every difficulty can be
taken care of.

234
00:37:00,687 --> 00:37:03,327
Inshallah, my sheik.

235
00:37:03,556 --> 00:37:07,556
Cerkutay can't die.

236
00:37:31,522 --> 00:37:35,522
Lovers can't die.

237
00:37:35,797 --> 00:37:39,797
Lovers can't die.

238
00:37:42,339 --> 00:37:46,339
I can't, Kumral Abdal.

239
00:37:46,768 --> 00:37:51,228
-It's the only reason.
-Stop havering.

240
00:37:51,912 --> 00:37:56,282
Mashallah, you have nine lives.

241
00:38:07,643 --> 00:38:11,643
You can't stop it because
you are healed.

242
00:38:11,643 --> 00:38:15,643
You will drink these
forever.

243
00:38:21,693 --> 00:38:25,693
Thank you, Kumral Abdal.

244
00:38:29,131 --> 00:38:33,131
Mashallah, back then...

245
00:38:33,131 --> 00:38:37,131
you healed hearts with
your words...

246
00:38:37,131 --> 00:38:41,131
now, you spread healing
with your skillful hands.

247
00:38:41,131 --> 00:38:46,611
Sush! What skill?
Don't say such things again!

248
00:38:47,549 --> 00:38:51,549
My Allah! Everyone has
wise people around them...

249
00:38:51,549 --> 00:38:55,549
I only attract crazy people
or traitors.

250
00:38:55,888 --> 00:38:59,888
Give me patience, my Allah.

251
00:39:00,997 --> 00:39:03,887
There are important news.

252
00:39:09,806 --> 00:39:14,286
Tell me, Gökçe.
What is it?

253
00:39:15,670 --> 00:39:19,670
I eavesdropped on Bala and
Gökçe Hatun.

254
00:39:21,578 --> 00:39:26,018
-Bala Hatun is pregnant.
-Pregnant?

255
00:40:40,569 --> 00:40:42,253
My Allah...

256
00:40:44,088 --> 00:40:46,489
My Allah...

257
00:40:48,218 --> 00:40:50,678
My Allah, what a difficult
test is this?

258
00:41:03,086 --> 00:41:06,474
I was the ornament of Umur Tribe.

259
00:41:07,246 --> 00:41:10,010
I was the dearie of my father.

260
00:41:10,871 --> 00:41:14,499
I accepted to be the second
wife of a brave man...

261
00:41:14,840 --> 00:41:18,318
only because his first wife
couldn't get pregnant.

262
00:41:20,439 --> 00:41:23,203
I wanted the tribes to be united.

263
00:41:23,458 --> 00:41:26,618
I wanted the Turks to be united.

264
00:41:34,621 --> 00:41:38,679
''If I'll have a child, let it be
from Osman Bey.''

265
00:41:46,123 --> 00:41:48,748
My Allah...

266
00:41:50,218 --> 00:41:52,885
My Allah...

267
00:42:05,660 --> 00:42:08,771
Why did they hide it?

268
00:42:11,580 --> 00:42:12,979
Are they...

269
00:42:28,483 --> 00:42:30,125
My son...

270
00:42:32,289 --> 00:42:33,542
My son...

271
00:42:35,378 --> 00:42:36,856
My son...

272
00:42:44,947 --> 00:42:46,751
What if it's a boy?

273
00:43:10,649 --> 00:43:13,267
İnegöl Castle

274
00:43:29,676 --> 00:43:31,797
Dear Rogatos!

275
00:43:46,600 --> 00:43:48,481
How are you?

276
00:43:48,679 --> 00:43:51,839
You should ask yourself.
You don't look well.

277
00:43:53,522 --> 00:43:55,419
It's a terrible day.

278
00:43:55,809 --> 00:43:59,781
Maybe it's not the day but
your perspective?

279
00:44:01,069 --> 00:44:05,415
Because your terrible day might
be a glorious one for another, right?

280
00:44:11,313 --> 00:44:13,911
Behold!
Nikola, the lord of İnegöl!

281
00:44:20,514 --> 00:44:22,514
Magnificus!

282
00:44:25,453 --> 00:44:28,518
He thinks he is Caesar.

283
00:44:34,465 --> 00:44:37,924
Finally, my friends. Finally!
Kosses!

284
00:44:41,224 --> 00:44:44,896
You are solid as a rock, like always.

285
00:44:46,574 --> 00:44:48,513
Rogatos!

286
00:44:51,406 --> 00:44:55,267
You have foxes in your head again.

287
00:44:55,409 --> 00:44:59,153
Our friend is having a terrible day.

288
00:44:59,926 --> 00:45:01,842
I know.

289
00:45:04,389 --> 00:45:06,130
Come.

290
00:45:17,943 --> 00:45:21,877
Rogatos' close friend and relative,
Gregor...

291
00:45:22,345 --> 00:45:25,191
have escaped from the emperor's
dungeon.

292
00:45:30,922 --> 00:45:35,865
And someone took him on his
way to Rogatos.

293
00:45:37,385 --> 00:45:39,172
Did I get it right?

294
00:45:40,903 --> 00:45:44,978
You want to protect a traitor who is
wanted by Emperor Andronicus.

295
00:45:44,978 --> 00:45:48,245
Is this right, Rogatos?

296
00:45:50,631 --> 00:45:52,815
Aren't you afraid?

297
00:45:54,216 --> 00:45:57,740
Father Gregor might be
a traitor for now.

298
00:45:58,125 --> 00:46:02,028
But this is life, he might turn
into a hero tomorrow.

299
00:46:07,026 --> 00:46:11,868
My old friend loves protecting
heroes.

300
00:46:13,175 --> 00:46:16,886
''They are the agents of Jesus
on earth.

301
00:46:18,212 --> 00:46:21,935
Those who protect them will accompany
Jesus in heaven.''

302
00:46:25,704 --> 00:46:30,267
Rogatos, you sound like someone
who wants to be a saint.

303
00:46:33,667 --> 00:46:37,012
But, know this...

304
00:46:37,287 --> 00:46:40,407
I will find out where
Father Gregor is.

305
00:46:41,665 --> 00:46:45,108
And when I do, I will take him.

306
00:46:45,375 --> 00:46:48,123
If only you knew...

307
00:46:48,374 --> 00:46:52,182
how much I would like to
have that Father.

308
00:46:52,902 --> 00:46:55,613
Dear, Rogatos.

309
00:46:57,326 --> 00:47:02,787
But unfortunately, I don't have him.

310
00:47:03,083 --> 00:47:06,243
Otherwise, I would like you to
be with Jesus in heaven.

311
00:47:13,588 --> 00:47:14,773
Yes.

312
00:47:16,503 --> 00:47:20,158
If none of us have Gregor...

313
00:47:20,946 --> 00:47:23,152
then, who has him?

314
00:47:31,805 --> 00:47:34,232
Of course, Osman is our primary
suspect.

315
00:47:34,799 --> 00:47:37,086
Osman, the Bey of the Kayı.

316
00:47:40,479 --> 00:47:45,608
The one that you always fail to beat...

317
00:47:47,784 --> 00:47:49,472
Right, Nikola?

318
00:48:08,013 --> 00:48:11,560
Master Gregor, what will we do now?

319
00:48:11,560 --> 00:48:16,154
We wanted to flee from the emperor,
now we are in the hands of the heathens.

320
00:48:16,404 --> 00:48:20,915
-Was it all for this?
-Your fuss won't help us, Andreas.

321
00:48:21,766 --> 00:48:23,685
You need to be calm.

322
00:48:24,030 --> 00:48:26,750
Will we stay idle, Master Gregor?

323
00:48:26,750 --> 00:48:29,807
If we know why we are here,
we can find a way out of here.

324
00:48:30,272 --> 00:48:32,966
How did Osman know about us?

325
00:48:33,304 --> 00:48:35,684
How did he know that we were coming?

326
00:48:40,394 --> 00:48:43,153
May your evening be good, Father.

327
00:48:43,153 --> 00:48:45,933
Your words are sweet but your power
is keeping us captive.

328
00:48:46,063 --> 00:48:49,345
This evil can only be expected
by a man like you.

329
00:48:50,883 --> 00:48:53,780
Captivity is difficult.
I know it well.

330
00:48:54,504 --> 00:48:57,999
I was tortured in your dungeons.

331
00:48:58,307 --> 00:49:02,039
But let's not call this
captivity.

332
00:49:02,039 --> 00:49:04,363
We are hosting you.

333
00:49:04,363 --> 00:49:07,772
So, it's our destiny to spend time
in the heart of the devil.

334
00:49:08,303 --> 00:49:12,599
What I wonder is, how has that
devil heard of us?

335
00:49:12,791 --> 00:49:15,001
How does the devil know us?

336
00:49:16,639 --> 00:49:20,592
You fleed from the devil's lap,
Father.

337
00:49:21,459 --> 00:49:26,852
You wouldn't be here if you were brave
against that devil...

338
00:49:27,116 --> 00:49:32,317
who imprisoned you, who blinded
the Patriarch.

339
00:49:40,373 --> 00:49:43,168
You know everything.

340
00:49:43,703 --> 00:49:48,031
I know how the Byzantine Emperor...

341
00:49:48,031 --> 00:49:52,914
gave you and the Patriarch orders,
to unite the Orthodoxes and Catholics...

342
00:49:52,914 --> 00:49:55,219
for the Pope's support.

343
00:49:58,092 --> 00:50:02,846
I know how the Patriarch was blinded
for refusing.

344
00:50:07,893 --> 00:50:11,666
I know how they tortured you
in that dungeon.

345
00:50:20,662 --> 00:50:23,346
And I know...

346
00:50:23,825 --> 00:50:26,592
how eager you were
to escape there.

347
00:51:03,717 --> 00:51:07,833
I know how you fought like
a man, too.

348
00:51:25,748 --> 00:51:29,298
You deserved heaven, my loyal
friend.

349
00:51:29,298 --> 00:51:32,188
You will be reborn with Christ's
companions. Give me your name.

350
00:51:32,188 --> 00:51:35,808
The secret is revealed, sir.
The secret is revealed.

351
00:51:35,808 --> 00:51:40,358
If you reveal the secret,
you know everything, Father.

352
00:51:42,180 --> 00:51:46,180
-What do you want from us?
-Just like this.

353
00:51:47,145 --> 00:51:50,545
Now, listen to me.

354
00:51:51,345 --> 00:51:55,495
Osman kidnapping the Father
doesn't sound possible to me.

355
00:51:55,694 --> 00:51:59,694
But you know him better, Nikola.

356
00:51:59,694 --> 00:52:04,044
You've seen him in battles.
Tell us now.

357
00:52:04,044 --> 00:52:07,164
What kind of a man is Osman?

358
00:52:08,703 --> 00:52:11,103
Osman...

359
00:52:11,436 --> 00:52:17,116
how could he know our internal affairs
that he can know the Father?

360
00:52:17,243 --> 00:52:21,243
If Osman sees the greatness of his
prey...

361
00:52:21,243 --> 00:52:26,703
he'll turn into a Father, a shepherd
anything, Rogatos.

362
00:52:29,866 --> 00:52:33,866
My God. It's been a while...

363
00:52:33,866 --> 00:52:37,866
since we faced the enemy but...

364
00:52:37,866 --> 00:52:40,946
I didn't know that Osman turned into
such a dangerous devil.

365
00:52:40,946 --> 00:52:44,056
I do.

366
00:52:44,203 --> 00:52:48,453
After all, you left me all alone
in this war, Kosses.

367
00:52:52,412 --> 00:52:57,472
I waved the Byzantine flag
alone.

368
00:52:57,876 --> 00:53:02,686
But you fought and fought to
be Caesar, Nikola.

369
00:53:02,686 --> 00:53:07,236
Understand it, this isn't Rome.

370
00:53:08,524 --> 00:53:12,524
A bit of love, a bit of wine...

371
00:53:12,524 --> 00:53:16,204
a bit of trade. Am I wrong?

372
00:53:19,038 --> 00:53:22,038
You don't understand.

373
00:53:22,440 --> 00:53:26,440
Osman is growing,
in lands...

374
00:53:26,440 --> 00:53:30,440
in people, in power...
He is growing!

375
00:53:30,440 --> 00:53:34,440
Soon, he'll turn into a snake that will
eat us all!

376
00:53:35,404 --> 00:53:39,404
If we don't unite...

377
00:53:39,404 --> 00:53:44,654
we'll all vanish soon.

378
00:53:49,526 --> 00:53:52,736
Then...

379
00:53:53,183 --> 00:53:56,143
We'll strengthen our unity.

380
00:53:56,143 --> 00:54:00,143
But Osman shouldn't see or hear
us.

381
00:54:01,802 --> 00:54:05,802
He should think that we
have a problem.

382
00:54:05,802 --> 00:54:09,802
Otherwise, Osman will...

383
00:54:09,802 --> 00:54:13,802
make us fight each other with
his devilry.

384
00:54:18,285 --> 00:54:22,285
For Byzantine!
For Byzantine!

385
00:54:22,285 --> 00:54:25,025
For Byzantine.

386
00:54:32,941 --> 00:54:36,941
You convinced me, Nikola.

387
00:54:36,941 --> 00:54:40,941
By saying that Osman has...

388
00:54:40,941 --> 00:54:45,311
Father Gregor, you convinced me.

389
00:54:51,978 --> 00:54:55,978
I will visit him tomorrow.

390
00:54:55,978 --> 00:54:59,978
He'll deny it.

391
00:55:02,615 --> 00:55:06,225
I'll understand it from his eyes.

392
00:55:09,316 --> 00:55:13,316
The children of Christ will attack
when they hear about this.

393
00:55:14,723 --> 00:55:18,963
-They'll burn your tribe.
-I know you to be smart.

394
00:55:22,414 --> 00:55:26,414
Don't make me doubt that.

395
00:55:26,848 --> 00:55:30,338
Control your anger.

396
00:55:30,338 --> 00:55:34,468
Don't forget that the Latins
came for Jerusalem.

397
00:55:35,475 --> 00:55:39,945
They killed their co-religionists,
the Orthodoxes.

398
00:55:40,413 --> 00:55:44,413
They tyrannized there.

399
00:55:46,469 --> 00:55:50,139
What do you want from me?

400
00:55:51,918 --> 00:55:55,918
-To trust me.
-You? You!

401
00:55:56,684 --> 00:55:59,934
To my devil?

402
00:56:00,192 --> 00:56:04,192
I know that trust can't be gained
over a night.

403
00:56:04,192 --> 00:56:08,942
But I say it tonight.
Know what I want.

404
00:56:09,153 --> 00:56:13,943
Know it. Your eyes will
start to see the truth soon.

405
00:56:14,235 --> 00:56:17,735
I will never trust you before
Christ comes down from the sky.

406
00:56:17,735 --> 00:56:19,835
Do you understand?

407
00:56:19,835 --> 00:56:23,835
This bed will do good.

408
00:56:28,136 --> 00:56:32,136
Good night now.

409
00:56:38,375 --> 00:56:42,375
Your eyes will spread fire.

410
00:56:42,375 --> 00:56:46,145
Your hands will hold swords.

411
00:56:46,145 --> 00:56:50,144
The enemies will lose their minds
for seeing you.

412
00:56:53,842 --> 00:56:57,192
It will happen, right, son?

413
00:56:57,879 --> 00:57:02,719
It will. It will.

414
00:57:02,719 --> 00:57:07,619
Your grandfather Ertuğrul Ghazi
will watch over you.

415
00:57:21,986 --> 00:57:25,526
Malhun Sultan.

416
00:57:25,694 --> 00:57:29,314
You are ready.

417
00:57:31,435 --> 00:57:35,025
You kept me waiting, Malhun Hatun.

418
00:57:35,025 --> 00:57:39,025
Is it bad, my bey?
You were with Orhan.

419
00:57:39,169 --> 00:57:42,869
Thank Allah.
Thank Allah.

420
00:57:42,869 --> 00:57:47,169
-My bey.
-I'm listening, Malhun.

421
00:57:47,437 --> 00:57:50,487
How is the love of a child?

422
00:57:51,070 --> 00:57:56,390
It's great. Great.
Really is.

423
00:58:00,674 --> 00:58:05,254
Thanks to you, I have a child.
Thank you.

424
00:58:09,201 --> 00:58:13,201
Inshallah, you'll have
many children.

425
00:58:23,331 --> 00:58:28,231
Come on. Let's not keep
the people waiting.

426
00:58:40,402 --> 00:58:42,672
Behold!

427
00:58:52,844 --> 00:58:56,844
-Salam Alaikum.
-Alaikum Salam.

428
00:59:11,713 --> 00:59:16,663
Finally, his face is smiling.
Thank Allah.

429
00:59:17,507 --> 00:59:21,997
So is yours, Bala.
It really does.

430
00:59:42,461 --> 00:59:44,781
Come.

431
00:59:49,724 --> 00:59:52,944
Enjoy it.

432
00:59:53,413 --> 00:59:57,413
With the name of Allah.

433
01:00:16,436 --> 01:00:19,786
-Boran.
-My bey.

434
01:00:20,088 --> 01:00:23,128
Sing for us.

435
01:00:26,913 --> 01:00:29,057
Alright, my bey.

436
01:00:56,929 --> 01:01:06,959
We've done many charities.

437
01:01:06,959 --> 01:01:11,999
Come, let's make peace.

438
01:01:11,999 --> 01:01:17,029
Our horse is saddled.

439
01:01:17,029 --> 01:01:22,069
Thanks to Allah.

440
01:01:22,069 --> 01:01:28,989
We've done many charities.
We've done many charities.

441
01:01:28,989 --> 01:01:34,219
We are reborn to be a river,
risen up to be a waterfall.

442
01:01:34,219 --> 01:01:39,349
We looked at the sea.

443
01:01:39,349 --> 01:01:42,389
Thanks to Allah.

444
01:01:51,334 --> 01:01:56,374
We've done many charities.

445
01:01:56,374 --> 01:02:01,464
Enemies came and left.
We survived.

446
01:02:01,464 --> 01:02:06,314
We were at the doors of the lord.

447
01:02:06,314 --> 01:02:11,514
We've grown like a sycamore.

448
01:02:11,514 --> 01:02:15,514
Thanks to Allah.

449
01:02:15,514 --> 01:02:19,514
We've done many charities.

450
01:02:19,514 --> 01:02:24,344
The enemies came and left.
We survived.

451
01:02:24,344 --> 01:02:29,124
We've done many charities.

452
01:02:29,124 --> 01:02:34,134
The enemies came and left.
We survived.

453
01:02:34,134 --> 01:02:39,194
We survived.
Thanks to Allah.

454
01:02:40,534 --> 01:02:44,534
Mashallah to my brother.

455
01:02:45,239 --> 01:02:49,239
Thank you.
May Allah bless your hands.

456
01:02:50,454 --> 01:02:54,454
Thank you, my bey.
Thank you.

457
01:02:57,005 --> 01:03:02,775
Today, here, we gathered
for my son Orhan's 40th day.

458
01:03:06,392 --> 01:03:11,002
My son in the bundle, Orhan...

459
01:03:11,432 --> 01:03:15,652
and many other sons and daughters
like him, expect something from us.

460
01:03:16,603 --> 01:03:19,493
What is it?

461
01:03:20,343 --> 01:03:25,243
We'll teach them our traditions
and Islamic morals.

462
01:03:26,105 --> 01:03:30,105
We exist from ancient times.

463
01:03:30,105 --> 01:03:35,065
But whenever something bad happened
to us, it's because we forgot our customs.

464
01:03:37,125 --> 01:03:40,355
It's because our morals got corrupted.

465
01:03:41,663 --> 01:03:47,163
If we forget it, we turn into the enemy.

466
01:03:47,499 --> 01:03:51,499
If we forget it, we'll lose...

467
01:03:52,455 --> 01:03:55,815
before fighting in the field.

468
01:03:55,897 --> 01:03:59,897
For this reason, it's all our
responsibility.

469
01:03:59,897 --> 01:04:03,897
May Allah give us good
sons...

470
01:04:03,897 --> 01:04:07,897
and good daughters.
-Amin.

471
01:04:34,381 --> 01:04:38,381
How is your health, Pretty-eyed?

472
01:04:39,018 --> 01:04:43,018
Does my child show its existence?

473
01:04:43,340 --> 01:04:46,450
Wouldn't it?

474
01:04:46,450 --> 01:04:50,450
It's already certain that it will be a
child of its father.

475
01:04:50,736 --> 01:04:54,016
It started early.

476
01:04:56,375 --> 01:05:00,015
What do you want it to be?

477
01:05:01,568 --> 01:05:06,268
I want a daughter from Allah.
A daughter is a companion to the father.

478
01:05:06,268 --> 01:05:10,268
Daughters love their fathers.

479
01:05:10,268 --> 01:05:14,268
I want to comb her hair just like this.

480
01:05:14,268 --> 01:05:18,268
I want her to set a table for me.

481
01:05:18,268 --> 01:05:22,268
I want her to take your hands...

482
01:05:22,268 --> 01:05:26,268
so that she can liven our tribe up.

483
01:05:30,704 --> 01:05:35,564
Mount a horse, hold a sword, fight
a battle too.

484
01:05:35,564 --> 01:05:39,664
That's for certain.
The mother is Bala Hatun.

485
01:05:46,084 --> 01:05:50,764
Tell me. When do we tell
the people?

486
01:05:55,523 --> 01:05:59,523
If you allow me, I want to tell
my father first.

487
01:05:59,526 --> 01:06:04,256
-I want to tell him tomorrow.
-Alright.

488
01:06:05,246 --> 01:06:08,296
Alright.

489
01:06:09,735 --> 01:06:14,315
Orhan? Orhan!

490
01:06:19,971 --> 01:06:24,431
Orhan! My son!

491
01:06:24,827 --> 01:06:27,387
Orhan!

492
01:06:29,016 --> 01:06:32,436
Orhan!

493
01:06:41,161 --> 01:06:45,161
-Brother!
-Brother Orhan!

494
01:07:18,472 --> 01:07:21,512
Orhan!

495
01:07:21,887 --> 01:07:24,837
Orhan...

496
01:07:38,153 --> 01:07:41,243
Orhan...

497
01:07:42,087 --> 01:07:45,277
Orhan!

498
01:07:45,847 --> 01:07:49,847
Orhan! My son!

499
01:07:49,847 --> 01:07:53,847
Orhan! Orhan!

500
01:07:53,847 --> 01:07:57,847
My son! No!

501
01:07:58,308 --> 01:08:01,568
My son!

502
01:08:04,902 --> 01:08:08,572
Orhan!

503
01:08:08,572 --> 01:08:11,082
My son.

504
01:08:20,447 --> 01:08:23,207
Bala?

505
01:08:35,377 --> 01:08:38,337
Bala!

506
01:08:42,059 --> 01:08:45,578
My son!

507
01:08:46,917 --> 01:08:50,377
My son!

508
01:08:52,310 --> 01:08:54,830
My son...

509
01:09:07,011 --> 01:09:11,011
My Allah!

510
01:09:26,673 --> 01:09:29,473
My son...

511
01:09:30,006 --> 01:09:34,456
My son... My Orhan...

512
01:09:44,220 --> 01:09:46,491
My son.

513
01:09:47,205 --> 01:09:50,484
May Allah protect me.

514
01:09:57,400 --> 01:10:02,160
With the ninety-nine names
of Allah...

515
01:10:02,160 --> 01:10:08,140
who creates as he wants and
fulfills our hearts with faith.

516
01:10:11,006 --> 01:10:15,616
Since the last year, we fought a lot.

517
01:10:15,616 --> 01:10:20,796
But our enemies underestimated us.
Osman isn't our match, they said.

518
01:10:22,063 --> 01:10:26,063
Since the last year...

519
01:10:26,063 --> 01:10:30,063
they were answered many times
on the field.

520
01:10:30,063 --> 01:10:33,293
Thank Allah.
Thank Allah.

521
01:10:33,293 --> 01:10:38,063
Osman Bey, with the prosperity
of the last year...

522
01:10:38,063 --> 01:10:42,063
all Turkmens are moving here.

523
01:10:42,063 --> 01:10:46,063
-Our Bey is hope for them.
-Indeed.

524
01:10:46,063 --> 01:10:50,063
The mountains are full with
Turkmen tents.

525
01:10:50,063 --> 01:10:53,613
They are all our friends and relatives.

526
01:10:53,613 --> 01:10:56,563
-They all are praying for you.
-Thank you.

527
01:10:57,823 --> 01:11:01,553
Mashallah but I'm worried, Osman Bey.

528
01:11:01,553 --> 01:11:05,203
Are you worried that we are a hope
for the Turkmens, Gündüz Bey?

529
01:11:06,600 --> 01:11:12,750
You will hear what you say, Boran Alp.

530
01:11:17,426 --> 01:11:22,426
This is the council.
You will think before speaking.

531
01:11:25,003 --> 01:11:29,003
It's hard to understand the lovers,
Gündüz Bey.

532
01:11:29,408 --> 01:11:32,348
Don't despise him.

533
01:11:34,716 --> 01:11:38,716
Brother, tell us.

534
01:11:38,986 --> 01:11:42,116
I will, brother.

535
01:11:42,116 --> 01:11:46,116
Our Turkmen brothers are coming.
They are welcome.

536
01:11:46,116 --> 01:11:50,496
But if we can't manage this
with our heads...

537
01:11:50,496 --> 01:11:53,226
it will burn us.

538
01:11:53,555 --> 01:11:58,515
You are right, brother.
Tell us what you heard.

539
01:11:58,515 --> 01:12:03,735
Many warriors are acting on their
own on the borders.

540
01:12:03,984 --> 01:12:08,174
They are having relationships
with the lords without us.

541
01:12:09,986 --> 01:12:13,986
They even raid their lands.

542
01:12:13,986 --> 01:12:17,986
Osman Bey, Byzantine schemes
never end.

543
01:12:17,986 --> 01:12:22,726
Tomorrow, they can send one of those
strong warriors to face us.

544
01:12:22,726 --> 01:12:26,686
Then, we'll have to spill
brothers' blood.

545
01:12:26,686 --> 01:12:31,196
I heard it too. A warrior named
Turgut Alp...

546
01:12:31,196 --> 01:12:35,766
already fights the lord of Harmankaya.
There are many like him, my bey.

547
01:13:10,253 --> 01:13:12,843
Where are you?

548
01:13:26,857 --> 01:13:31,347
My brother. Why did he
call me so suddenly?

549
01:13:31,807 --> 01:13:37,577
-Don't you think it's strange, Cornelia?
-Maybe it's longing, my lady.

550
01:13:38,606 --> 01:13:44,256
No, Cornelia. He would come
himself then.

551
01:13:46,641 --> 01:13:50,641
Whatever it is, it must be important.

552
01:13:50,641 --> 01:13:55,581
Everyone knows how much your brother
loves you. Even his enemies.

553
01:13:58,195 --> 01:14:03,175
Cornelia. Is this why you
are anxious like this?

554
01:14:03,830 --> 01:14:08,690
Who can hurt Kosses' sister?
We are guarded by many men.

555
01:14:25,623 --> 01:14:29,033
We'll charge altogether.

556
01:14:29,033 --> 01:14:33,033
You won't hesitate, you won't stumble.

557
01:14:33,455 --> 01:14:37,455
If a horse gets afraid and flees...

558
01:14:41,774 --> 01:14:45,961
-We need her alive.
-Alright, Turgut Bey!

559
01:15:02,506 --> 01:15:07,864
We are under attack!

560
01:16:09,460 --> 01:16:13,181
-My lady!
-Alright, stay calm.

561
01:18:15,224 --> 01:18:19,224
Harmankaya's lord Michael Kosses'
dearie.

562
01:18:21,740 --> 01:18:25,190
Welcome, Marie.

563
01:18:33,737 --> 01:18:36,587
It's my order.

564
01:18:36,587 --> 01:18:40,587
All new nomads will be visited.

565
01:18:40,587 --> 01:18:44,887
Without my order, no one
mounts a horse.

566
01:18:45,205 --> 01:18:49,355
Without an order, no one
wields a sword.

567
01:18:49,355 --> 01:18:54,355
If my order gets
ignored...

568
01:18:55,937 --> 01:18:59,937
they should be remembered of what
will happen.

569
01:18:59,937 --> 01:19:01,737
Alright, my bey.

570
01:19:02,866 --> 01:19:06,306
Thank you.

571
01:19:09,985 --> 01:19:12,675
Alright.

572
01:19:22,509 --> 01:19:27,749
My bey, Rogaros, the lord of
Bilecik is here. He wants audience.

573
01:19:29,006 --> 01:19:33,006
Good. Good.

574
01:19:39,327 --> 01:19:43,327
-What is this, brother?
-Something good.

575
01:19:43,441 --> 01:19:45,761
Something good.

576
01:19:59,636 --> 01:20:01,306
Welcome, Rogatus.

577
01:20:02,989 --> 01:20:04,589
Thank you, Osman Bey.

578
01:20:06,274 --> 01:20:09,134
Harmankaya Castle

579
01:20:38,142 --> 01:20:39,742
Lord Kosses!

580
01:20:41,887 --> 01:20:44,057
The crew that was bringing your Mari...

581
01:20:47,880 --> 01:20:49,460
...they were raided, Sir.

582
01:20:51,994 --> 01:20:54,114
They kidnapped your sister.

583
01:21:07,033 --> 01:21:10,913
The Bey of those Turks we imprisoned...

584
01:21:11,368 --> 01:21:13,548
... Turgut Alp.

585
01:21:13,996 --> 01:21:15,886
He kidnapped her!

586
01:21:16,941 --> 01:21:20,441
In return for their worthless alps...

587
01:21:20,511 --> 01:21:22,351
...my sister.

588
01:21:23,127 --> 01:21:24,357
Is that so?

589
01:21:25,865 --> 01:21:27,445
What will we do, Sir?

590
01:21:30,000 --> 01:21:31,790
What will we do?

591
01:21:36,757 --> 01:21:39,707
We will bring their world collapse
around them.

592
01:21:41,796 --> 01:21:44,556
We will crucify them.

593
01:21:45,484 --> 01:21:48,094
We will rip out their lungs.

594
01:21:49,289 --> 01:21:52,159
We will rip out and take their lungs.

595
01:21:55,582 --> 01:21:58,582
So, how will we take Mari back, Sir?

596
01:22:02,219 --> 01:22:04,039
Who kills only one bird...

597
01:22:05,680 --> 01:22:08,120
...with one stone...

598
01:22:09,035 --> 01:22:11,115
... is either a fool...

599
01:22:14,476 --> 01:22:16,336
...or a shepherd.

600
01:22:18,980 --> 01:22:21,550
I am not that stupid Nikola.

601
01:22:21,992 --> 01:22:24,242
I will play such a game to them that...

602
01:22:25,488 --> 01:22:28,688
... with every step they take to
solve it...

603
01:22:29,067 --> 01:22:31,407
...they will come closer to
becoming my prey.

604
01:22:33,786 --> 01:22:35,916
Prepare a gift for Osman Bey.

605
01:22:36,692 --> 01:22:38,562
We will pay him a visit.

606
01:22:40,145 --> 01:22:42,735
Let's meet him already.

607
01:22:43,760 --> 01:22:45,290
What shall we prepare for him?

608
01:22:48,640 --> 01:22:51,520
Of course, the Turks' favorite.

609
01:22:54,432 --> 01:22:55,592
Sure!

610
01:23:08,040 --> 01:23:12,920
I am here to protect the friendship that
has been going on since Lord Leo...

611
01:23:13,671 --> 01:23:15,371
...and your father Ertuğrul Gazi.

612
01:23:15,962 --> 01:23:16,982
Good.

613
01:23:17,624 --> 01:23:19,574
You did well, Lord Rogatus.

614
01:23:20,103 --> 01:23:21,523
We want the same as well.

615
01:23:22,442 --> 01:23:29,482
We know that as Tekfus Leo, you too come
from the Laskarid Dynasty.

616
01:23:30,630 --> 01:23:36,950
This means you don't have a friendship
with the Emperor or the Lords.

617
01:23:40,825 --> 01:23:42,345
You are right.

618
01:23:43,389 --> 01:23:47,069
I hope our friendship will last for life.

619
01:23:49,656 --> 01:23:51,466
I'd like to ask you something.

620
01:23:53,988 --> 01:24:00,178
Father Gregor, who was supposed to be
under my protection...

621
01:24:00,178 --> 01:24:04,532
...but unfortunately was taken from me.

622
01:24:06,076 --> 01:24:07,486
I am looking for him.

623
01:24:11,000 --> 01:24:14,830
We don't know who took him.

624
01:24:17,709 --> 01:24:20,409
Do you have any information on the matter,
Osman Bey?

625
01:24:23,458 --> 01:24:26,838
What would I do with a priest or an exarch,
Rogatus.

626
01:24:29,330 --> 01:24:31,500
Why are you asking me this?

627
01:24:34,183 --> 01:24:36,433
As you said earlier...

628
01:24:36,921 --> 01:24:40,491
...I am not on good terms with the Emperor
or the Lords.

629
01:24:41,732 --> 01:24:44,122
Father Gregor escaped the Emperor.

630
01:24:45,384 --> 01:24:48,014
He was on the road to take refuge in me.

631
01:24:49,018 --> 01:24:52,198
Those who want our help are
much important to us, Osman Bey.

632
01:24:53,011 --> 01:24:55,841
Of course, those who want our help are
important to us too.

633
01:24:57,178 --> 01:25:00,038
But the priest trusted you and
tried to take refuge.

634
01:25:01,429 --> 01:25:05,989
I don't understand what does this have
to do with me.

635
01:25:08,253 --> 01:25:11,553
Are you going to ask everyone escaping
you to me, Rogatus?

636
01:25:14,233 --> 01:25:16,553
Father Gregor is my friend.

637
01:25:17,497 --> 01:25:19,297
I will find him, Osman Bey.

638
01:25:21,559 --> 01:25:23,849
Even though you are implying...

639
01:25:24,951 --> 01:25:26,601
...you are blaming me.

640
01:25:29,921 --> 01:25:32,261
However, you have many enemies.

641
01:25:34,949 --> 01:25:38,199
Your dynasty is enough for
the other Lords.

642
01:25:39,673 --> 01:25:41,263
Even for the Emperor.

643
01:25:42,668 --> 01:25:48,238
What makes you an enemy to them,
makes you a friend to me.

644
01:25:49,951 --> 01:25:51,851
We were friends with Lord Leo.

645
01:25:54,912 --> 01:25:57,102
We'd like to stay friends with you too.

646
01:25:58,138 --> 01:26:00,108
I hope, Osman Bey.

647
01:26:01,053 --> 01:26:02,513
I hope.

648
01:26:12,082 --> 01:26:13,842
May you be well.

649
01:26:22,773 --> 01:26:25,773
They come to the tribe and ask about
a priest.

650
01:26:27,034 --> 01:26:29,974
As if it is not enough, they blame us.

651
01:26:32,423 --> 01:26:34,903
I told. I did.

652
01:26:36,340 --> 01:26:39,390
This will not end for a while.
For a long while.

653
01:26:42,824 --> 01:26:44,674
If you'll excuse me, Osman Bey.

654
01:26:46,996 --> 01:26:48,506
What's done is done, brother.

655
01:26:50,024 --> 01:26:53,184
It was supposed to happen and it did.

656
01:26:54,110 --> 01:26:55,630
You keep cautious.

657
01:26:56,369 --> 01:26:58,119
Keep an eye open for the priest.

658
01:27:00,254 --> 01:27:01,874
As you command, my Bey.

659
01:27:28,457 --> 01:27:30,547
You are smiling!

660
01:27:32,589 --> 01:27:34,749
There is good news, obviously.

661
01:27:53,622 --> 01:27:55,102
Really?

662
01:27:57,473 --> 01:27:58,913
Thank goodness.

663
01:28:01,609 --> 01:28:05,759
My Rabb saw me, heard my cries.

664
01:28:10,930 --> 01:28:14,250
Made me a partner in the joy of
our Sare Valide, my Sheik.

665
01:28:14,926 --> 01:28:16,776
Put out the fire in me.

666
01:28:23,198 --> 01:28:25,558
I am going to be a mother, my Sheik.

667
01:28:29,112 --> 01:28:30,742
Thanks to Allah!

668
01:28:37,113 --> 01:28:38,833
Thanks to Allah!

669
01:28:46,265 --> 01:28:48,665
''In the name of Allah, the merciful.''

670
01:29:07,397 --> 01:29:09,647
“Allah is great and there is no god
but Allah.”

671
01:29:21,955 --> 01:29:24,225
"Allah hears those who praise Him."

672
01:29:25,648 --> 01:29:27,858
“Allah is great and there is no god
but Allah.”

673
01:29:32,143 --> 01:29:34,363
“Allah is great and there is no god
but Allah.”

674
01:29:44,728 --> 01:29:46,918
“Allah is great and there is no god
but Allah.”

675
01:29:52,266 --> 01:29:55,586
“Allah is great and there is no god
but Allah.”

676
01:30:12,432 --> 01:30:16,432
"May the peace of Allah be upon you"

677
01:30:36,730 --> 01:30:39,650
''In the name of Allah, the merciful.''

678
01:30:56,199 --> 01:30:58,579
Thanks to Allah!

679
01:30:58,849 --> 01:31:01,129
Thanks to Allah!

680
01:31:05,374 --> 01:31:10,794
You garnished your waiting with patience,
my beautiful girl.

681
01:31:13,291 --> 01:31:17,961
Allah granted you a child.

682
01:31:19,915 --> 01:31:22,225
With no doubt, he is the one hearing
the prayers.

683
01:31:24,499 --> 01:31:26,979
Even when I thought there was no remedy...

684
01:31:28,422 --> 01:31:31,462
... your words would heal my heart,
my Sheik.

685
01:31:35,787 --> 01:31:38,247
Now, you are also increasing my joy.

686
01:31:39,211 --> 01:31:44,651
My Almighty Allah has tested you with
the test of his servants whom he loves.

687
01:31:46,476 --> 01:31:49,456
You took the right road.

688
01:31:50,533 --> 01:31:57,733
You put your Bey, your tribe and the world
of Islam first.

689
01:32:02,598 --> 01:32:06,598
Your joy is your reward.

690
01:32:10,344 --> 01:32:12,904
When should I announce it to the tribe,
my Sheik?

691
01:32:20,447 --> 01:32:22,497
There is time, my dear.

692
01:32:23,341 --> 01:32:25,041
There is time.

693
01:32:32,310 --> 01:32:36,310
Turgut Bey Tribe

694
01:32:49,418 --> 01:32:53,598
- Welcome, my Bey!
- Welcome Bey!

695
01:33:21,999 --> 01:33:23,309
Kutay.

696
01:33:56,750 --> 01:33:59,790
You will pay for this, you vile barbarian!

697
01:34:01,591 --> 01:34:03,101
Barbarian?

698
01:34:07,863 --> 01:34:11,863
You are this barbarian's guest until I get
my alps back, Rumelian beauty.

699
01:35:48,386 --> 01:35:49,836
Lord Kosses.

700
01:35:51,689 --> 01:35:53,249
Welcome.

701
01:35:54,943 --> 01:35:56,363
Thank you, Alp.

702
01:35:59,452 --> 01:36:01,252
I demand a meeting with Osman Bey.

703
01:36:03,268 --> 01:36:05,148
He knows you were coming.

704
01:36:08,127 --> 01:36:09,297
Alps!

705
01:36:31,751 --> 01:36:33,311
Are you available, my Bey?

706
01:36:37,475 --> 01:36:38,695
Come in.

707
01:37:14,472 --> 01:37:16,272
Welcome, Mikhael Kosses.

708
01:37:19,882 --> 01:37:21,342
What is it?

709
01:37:23,893 --> 01:37:27,363
I brought a very precious Andalusian horse
for your son Orhan.

710
01:37:27,803 --> 01:37:29,353
Like you say...

711
01:37:29,690 --> 01:37:31,420
...the horse is a Turk's wing.

712
01:37:31,852 --> 01:37:33,522
I hope you will like it, Osman Bey.

713
01:37:33,556 --> 01:37:36,766
And your son may fly freely to wherever
he wants.

714
01:37:37,228 --> 01:37:39,988
Thank you, thank you.

715
01:37:42,903 --> 01:37:45,393
Lord Rogatus Laskaris came today.

716
01:37:46,656 --> 01:37:49,056
He mentioned someone named Father Gregor.

717
01:37:49,808 --> 01:37:51,808
I guess you came for him too.

718
01:37:54,379 --> 01:37:55,979
Here you go.

719
01:37:56,499 --> 01:37:59,989
I wish that was the case, Osman Bey.

720
01:38:01,124 --> 01:38:05,774
Neither Rogatus nor Father Gregor...
I don't care about them, Osman Bey.

721
01:38:09,207 --> 01:38:11,007
What is the matter, then?

722
01:38:12,985 --> 01:38:14,735
My sister.

723
01:38:17,047 --> 01:38:20,487
The convoy that was bringing my sister
Mari to me was raided.

724
01:38:21,391 --> 01:38:23,701
Who did it was a Turkoman Bey.

725
01:38:23,989 --> 01:38:25,269
Turgut Alp.

726
01:38:29,617 --> 01:38:31,257
You must know him.

727
01:38:34,601 --> 01:38:40,631
Is there a tradition of kidnapping women,
Osman Bey?

728
01:38:41,920 --> 01:38:47,020
Do you have a tradition of intercepting
a defenseless woman...

729
01:38:47,234 --> 01:38:48,824
... going home to her family?

730
01:38:52,772 --> 01:38:56,312
Do you have a tradition of drawing
a sword...

731
01:38:56,312 --> 01:38:59,012
...to those who don't have a sword,
Osman Bey?

732
01:38:59,107 --> 01:39:00,687
Stop.

733
01:39:08,768 --> 01:39:11,088
Be aware of your words, Kosses.

734
01:39:12,705 --> 01:39:14,715
I am.

735
01:39:15,214 --> 01:39:18,764
We know you as the leader of
all Turkmens in this area.

736
01:39:19,190 --> 01:39:25,380
We know that no Turkmen around borders
can fly a bird without your knowledge.

737
01:39:26,290 --> 01:39:29,640
Or do we know wrong?

738
01:39:30,298 --> 01:39:32,108
You know right, Kosses.

739
01:39:33,811 --> 01:39:37,811
I choose my friend and my enemy
myself.

740
01:39:39,864 --> 01:39:44,024
And I choose with whom I will stay friends
or enemies.

741
01:39:47,004 --> 01:39:49,364
They took my most precious from me.

742
01:39:50,669 --> 01:39:55,589
I don't know even if she is alive or not.

743
01:39:57,146 --> 01:39:59,706
I came here to ask for help from you.

744
01:40:04,074 --> 01:40:09,154
If I am not aware of my words, the reason
is clear.

745
01:40:11,709 --> 01:40:19,679
Whoever comes to my door and asks me
for help, especially for those in need...

746
01:40:22,207 --> 01:40:25,347
... doesn't leave without getting
what he asked for.

747
01:40:29,369 --> 01:40:30,989
Wait for my word.

748
01:40:33,173 --> 01:40:35,043
I will bring your sister to you.

749
01:40:36,207 --> 01:40:37,497
But...

750
01:40:37,692 --> 01:40:40,132
... meanwhile, if you make a mistake...

751
01:40:42,004 --> 01:40:44,244
... then you will incur my wrath.

752
01:40:47,053 --> 01:40:53,463
God is my witness that my only wish is to
get my sister back safe and sound.

753
01:40:58,836 --> 01:41:00,646
You are as much as they say.

754
01:41:03,683 --> 01:41:05,263
May God protect you.

755
01:41:13,813 --> 01:41:16,303
- Alps!
- My Bey.

756
01:41:18,527 --> 01:41:19,987
Make the preparations.

757
01:41:20,021 --> 01:41:21,801
Let's go to Turgut Alp.

758
01:41:22,501 --> 01:41:24,481
Let's meet him.

759
01:41:25,699 --> 01:41:28,639
Let's find out why he kidnapped Kosses'
sister Mari.

760
01:41:30,604 --> 01:41:32,904
Let's see what is behind this.

761
01:41:33,016 --> 01:41:35,636
- As you command, Bey!
- As you command, my Bey!

762
01:41:44,645 --> 01:41:48,645
Turgut Bey Tribe

763
01:42:04,905 --> 01:42:06,495
Destur, Hatun!

764
01:42:32,491 --> 01:42:35,701
You must be hungry.
Come on, eat.

765
01:42:35,774 --> 01:42:37,814
Do you want to poison us?

766
01:43:00,664 --> 01:43:02,514
Don't be afraid.

767
01:43:02,720 --> 01:43:04,580
Snake! Snake!

768
01:43:16,181 --> 01:43:18,331
Not me but...

769
01:43:21,481 --> 01:43:23,651
...someone else was going to poison you.

770
01:43:33,970 --> 01:43:35,930
You wait for gratitude.

771
01:43:37,412 --> 01:43:40,982
I will never be grateful to a barbarian
like you who treats women like this!

772
01:43:40,982 --> 01:43:42,482
Look, woman!

773
01:43:44,691 --> 01:43:46,461
My problem is not with you.

774
01:43:47,546 --> 01:43:50,796
Your brother Kosses imprisoned my alps.

775
01:43:52,063 --> 01:43:55,143
If your brother gives my alps back
safe and sound...

776
01:43:56,184 --> 01:43:57,994
...you can get out of here.

777
01:43:58,018 --> 01:44:00,298
My brother Kosses will make you pay
for this!

778
01:44:11,253 --> 01:44:12,933
Let him do so.

779
01:44:55,349 --> 01:44:59,349
Turgut Bey Tribe

780
01:45:01,948 --> 01:45:03,878
Hand holds the sword, Kutan.

781
01:45:04,444 --> 01:45:06,284
The arm connects the hand to the body.

782
01:45:06,809 --> 01:45:08,819
You are my right arm.

783
01:45:10,158 --> 01:45:12,198
You won't go to give this news.

784
01:45:13,138 --> 01:45:16,488
Kosses' wound is deep.
He will try to attack at every chance.

785
01:45:19,868 --> 01:45:22,808
Serhat!
To Lord Kosses.

786
01:46:12,388 --> 01:46:13,788
Turgut Alp!

787
01:46:14,090 --> 01:46:17,140
It's me!
Who is asking?

788
01:46:19,473 --> 01:46:22,363
The son of Ertuğrul Gazi, Bey of
the Kayı tribe, Osman Bey.

789
01:46:42,718 --> 01:46:46,178
Make way to your Osman Bey, alps!

790
01:47:15,818 --> 01:47:19,488
- Selamun Aleyküm.
-Aleyküm Selam.

791
01:47:19,516 --> 01:47:20,866
Welcome.

792
01:47:22,995 --> 01:47:26,755
The girl you kidnapped, Mari.

793
01:47:29,560 --> 01:47:32,370
Her brother, Lord of Harmankaya Mikhael
Kosses came to me.

794
01:47:34,595 --> 01:47:36,345
He wants his sister.

795
01:47:44,411 --> 01:47:46,071
Osman Bey.

796
01:47:46,973 --> 01:47:52,023
We know your name, your bravery,
and your power well.

797
01:47:53,184 --> 01:47:57,634
Just as you do all you do to protect
your tribe...

798
01:47:57,634 --> 01:47:59,424
...I do the same.

799
01:47:59,451 --> 01:48:02,361
Mikhael Kosses has my alps.

800
01:48:05,413 --> 01:48:08,973
I won't give Mari back until I see my alps
back in the tribe.

801
01:48:12,530 --> 01:48:16,530
Neither to you, Osman Bey, nor to anyone
else.

802
01:48:19,360 --> 01:48:22,520
If you know my name and bravery,
then you must also know...

803
01:48:23,150 --> 01:48:26,850
... you must trust my word, Turgut Alp.

804
01:48:31,161 --> 01:48:32,841
Give Mari to me.

805
01:48:34,785 --> 01:48:37,835
And I will take your alps back and give
them back to you.

806
01:48:39,507 --> 01:48:44,627
Therefore, I will be an intermediary in
the trade you will make anyway.

807
01:49:04,218 --> 01:49:09,668
-Kutan, bring the girls.
-As you command, my Bey.

808
01:49:40,111 --> 01:49:44,111
Osman Bey will take you to your brother
Kosses.

809
01:49:47,393 --> 01:49:49,353
But tell him.

810
01:49:51,270 --> 01:49:53,450
We will meet him one day.

811
01:49:55,641 --> 01:49:58,821
I will be there to watch when
that day comes.

812
01:50:01,318 --> 01:50:02,768
Come on, leave.

813
01:50:11,047 --> 01:50:12,727
You did the right thing.

814
01:50:31,171 --> 01:50:32,831
Osman Bey!

815
01:50:37,392 --> 01:50:40,242
I would like to know you as I did
before we met.

816
01:50:45,741 --> 01:50:47,741
A man of his word.

817
01:51:19,799 --> 01:51:21,479
Don't worry!

818
01:51:23,022 --> 01:51:25,262
We know you as one of us.

819
01:51:26,221 --> 01:51:28,641
You know us as you please.

820
01:51:33,151 --> 01:51:36,341
You will have your alps back as soon as
possible.

821
01:52:07,186 --> 01:52:09,126
-Boran.
-Yes, my Bey?

822
01:52:09,524 --> 01:52:10,934
Take Mari.

823
01:52:11,210 --> 01:52:13,530
And take back the alps of Turgut Alp.

824
01:52:14,671 --> 01:52:17,971
-But remain cautious.
-As you command, my Bey.

825
01:52:44,155 --> 01:52:48,155
Harmankaya Castle

826
01:53:09,099 --> 01:53:11,549
But we guaranteed our job.

827
01:53:13,917 --> 01:53:16,097
Forefinger...

828
01:53:18,272 --> 01:53:20,122
... and thumb.

829
01:53:23,806 --> 01:53:29,766
These hands can no longer hold a sword
or use a bow.

830
01:53:32,061 --> 01:53:34,251
You really guaranteed it, Sir.

831
01:53:35,221 --> 01:53:38,661
But my fear is that, as you know, they
have Mari.

832
01:53:38,661 --> 01:53:40,481
When he sees them like this--

833
01:53:40,487 --> 01:53:43,667
Of course, Osman Bey will come to us
with that request.

834
01:53:45,770 --> 01:53:51,610
He will say ''I brought you your sister
but Turgut also wants his alps back.''.

835
01:53:54,981 --> 01:53:57,761
And we won't upset him.

836
01:53:59,594 --> 01:54:01,434
We will give them back.

837
01:54:02,529 --> 01:54:04,899
Just with a little missing.

838
01:54:07,974 --> 01:54:10,644
Sir, one of Osman Bey's alps, Boran Alp
came.

839
01:54:10,644 --> 01:54:12,214
Your sister is with him, Sir.

840
01:54:16,486 --> 01:54:20,006
Osman Bey kept his promise quicker than
I expected.

841
01:54:40,719 --> 01:54:42,529
What will we do now, Master Gregor?

842
01:54:44,213 --> 01:54:45,973
How long will we stay here?

843
01:54:45,973 --> 01:54:47,963
We won't be wasting time, Andreas.

844
01:54:50,305 --> 01:54:53,185
We will find a way to inform
Lord Rogatus.

845
01:54:54,590 --> 01:54:56,510
We can't get out of here without him.

846
01:55:06,322 --> 01:55:10,322
-Andreas, the door.
-Of course, Sir.

847
01:55:58,572 --> 01:56:00,172
Are you well?

848
01:56:03,069 --> 01:56:04,899
It is well.

849
01:56:07,836 --> 01:56:09,826
We will live, Andreas.

850
01:56:11,343 --> 01:56:17,253
We will live and get rid of Osman for the
trust we are carrying.

851
01:56:30,885 --> 01:56:32,335
Brother!

852
01:56:38,775 --> 01:56:40,335
Are you alright?

853
01:56:40,845 --> 01:56:41,715
Come here.

854
01:56:46,381 --> 01:56:50,901
I owe Osman Bey for bringing my sister
to me safe and sound.

855
01:56:55,373 --> 01:56:57,823
We brought your sister
to you safe and sound.

856
01:57:00,366 --> 01:57:03,916
Now give us Turgut Bey's alps safe and
sound.

857
01:57:05,656 --> 01:57:09,086
You brought me my most precious.

858
01:57:09,978 --> 01:57:13,598
Nestor, set the imprisoned Turks free
immediately.

859
01:58:11,407 --> 01:58:14,717
Come on, my brothers!

860
01:58:14,717 --> 01:58:16,257
Come on!

861
01:58:16,257 --> 01:58:17,297
Brothers!

862
01:58:19,902 --> 01:58:21,802
Stay calm.

863
01:58:28,383 --> 01:58:30,221
What is this, Tekfus Kosses?

864
01:58:30,261 --> 01:58:34,341
Each bow they stretched cost the life
of one of my soldiers.

865
01:58:35,743 --> 01:58:41,463
I took two fingers from them for each
life they took.

866
01:58:46,920 --> 01:58:50,010
I think it is enough.
Right?

867
01:58:55,952 --> 01:58:59,952
Would you be satisfied with less,
Boran Alp?

868
01:59:13,457 --> 01:59:15,717
Send my gratitude to Osman Bey.

869
01:59:16,687 --> 01:59:19,197
Come on, have a safe trip.

870
01:59:19,287 --> 01:59:20,437
Mari.

871
01:59:32,750 --> 01:59:39,860
I remembered the past. How hard we tried
to weave various rugs with Hayme Ana.

872
01:59:40,944 --> 01:59:44,594
Poverty on one side,
the enemy on the other...

873
01:59:45,488 --> 01:59:47,758
Though, Turk's enemies never cease
to exist.

874
01:59:48,632 --> 01:59:51,902
Look, thankfully now we have
a great tribe.

875
01:59:52,225 --> 01:59:55,105
And these eyes had a chance to see
my Orhan.

876
01:59:56,324 --> 01:59:58,944
May Allah raise him with his mother
and father, my dear.

877
01:59:59,135 --> 02:00:02,915
May Allah grant him to be a son
worthy of his ancestors.

878
02:00:03,024 --> 02:00:04,384
Amen, mother.

879
02:00:04,868 --> 02:00:08,868
- Tell me, where is my Orhan? How's he?
- He is fine, thank Allah.

880
02:00:09,135 --> 02:00:12,045
He's asleep.

881
02:00:12,055 --> 02:00:15,885
He'll be a good kid.

882
02:00:18,053 --> 02:00:26,083
My daughter, thank Allah we have an heir.

883
02:00:27,659 --> 02:00:30,969
Inshallah you will have more children.

884
02:00:31,915 --> 02:00:34,545
Inshallah, mother.

885
02:00:36,730 --> 02:00:40,730
Selcan mother, I am curious
about something.

886
02:00:41,047 --> 02:00:44,007
You are an experienced woman.

887
02:00:44,367 --> 02:00:49,327
I always wondered whether my child
would be a girl or a boy.

888
02:00:49,726 --> 02:00:54,256
Some say...

889
02:00:54,370 --> 02:00:57,920
if you have a higher tummy, it will be
a girl...

890
02:00:57,943 --> 02:01:01,463
if you have a lower tummy, it
will be a boy.

891
02:01:01,730 --> 02:01:04,680
Yes, mine was low.

892
02:01:04,727 --> 02:01:08,727
Yes but it's not always true.

893
02:01:08,971 --> 02:01:11,791
They also say that if you
crave sweets, it's a boy...

894
02:01:11,908 --> 02:01:15,448
and if you crave sour
food, it's a girl.

895
02:01:19,866 --> 02:01:23,296
- Have a nice day, Hatuns.
- Thank you, Bala Hatun.

896
02:01:23,400 --> 02:01:27,400
- Welcome, Bala.
- Thank you, Selcan mother.

897
02:01:28,770 --> 02:01:31,970
Welcome, Bala Hatun.
Where are you coming from?

898
02:01:32,122 --> 02:01:36,122
I have visited my father.

899
02:01:36,540 --> 02:01:40,540
- Inshallah he's fine and healthy.
- Yes, thank Allah.

900
02:01:42,225 --> 02:01:46,415
I haven't seen you anywhere in the tent.

901
02:01:46,590 --> 02:01:49,410
What happened?

902
02:01:54,735 --> 02:01:58,315
Beys are at
the war, Hatuns are in the tent.

903
02:01:58,328 --> 02:02:03,188
I am so happy to see you like that.

904
02:02:03,864 --> 02:02:07,604
My daughters.
Mashallah.

905
02:02:11,109 --> 02:02:14,309
Turkmens trust Osman.

906
02:02:16,248 --> 02:02:22,208
He should be happy to gain their trust.

907
02:02:26,155 --> 02:02:31,205
He should feel comfortable in his tent.

908
02:02:35,788 --> 02:02:39,788
Don't be angry towards me for what I said.

909
02:02:41,234 --> 02:02:46,394
Be nice to each other.

910
02:02:48,021 --> 02:02:52,021
People will say lots of things if they
see you unhappy.

911
02:02:52,082 --> 02:02:56,082
Be protective over each other.

912
02:02:57,422 --> 02:03:02,772
May your sisterhood be infinite.

913
02:03:04,825 --> 02:03:08,095
- Thank you, mother.
- Thank you, mother.

914
02:03:08,139 --> 02:03:14,669
I'll wander around. Have a nice day.

915
02:03:15,415 --> 02:03:19,415
- Have a nice day, Hatuns.
- Thank you, Selcan Hatun.

916
02:03:29,138 --> 02:03:31,528
Are you pregnant?

917
02:03:32,519 --> 02:03:34,419
What?

918
02:03:47,258 --> 02:03:49,278
How do you know?

919
02:03:49,706 --> 02:03:53,706
- Is it true?
- Who told you that?

920
02:03:56,543 --> 02:03:59,783
I had a dream.

921
02:04:04,895 --> 02:04:11,035
You were holding a baby. Tell me.
Is it true?

922
02:04:20,201 --> 02:04:25,621
Mashallah. It's a miracle.
The miracle of Allah.

923
02:04:28,692 --> 02:04:33,332
- It'll be a comrade to my Orhan.
- Inshallah.

924
02:04:39,532 --> 02:04:43,532
I wanted to be sure. That's why I didn't
tell anyone.

925
02:04:44,358 --> 02:04:48,688
Thank Allah.

926
02:04:53,582 --> 02:04:58,092
Tell me, what do you crave?

927
02:05:00,077 --> 02:05:04,717
When I was pregnant, I craved sweets.
What do you want?

928
02:05:04,840 --> 02:05:07,930
Sweet food or sour food?

929
02:05:16,360 --> 02:05:21,780
Thank you, Malhun Hatun.
I don't crave anything.

930
02:05:25,316 --> 02:05:29,316
It's our secret, right?

931
02:05:29,790 --> 02:05:34,340
Don't tell anyone.
I want to be sure first.

932
02:05:35,904 --> 02:05:39,904
- Then we'll tell everyone.
- I know, Bala Hatun.

933
02:05:39,933 --> 02:05:43,933
Don't worry, it's our secret.

934
02:06:11,398 --> 02:06:12,568
It's a trap!

935
02:06:21,084 --> 02:06:24,464
Brothers, come on!

936
02:06:34,749 --> 02:06:38,749
Be careful, Alps!

937
02:06:55,913 --> 02:06:59,263
Come on, brothers!

938
02:08:02,615 --> 02:08:05,935
Brilliant.

939
02:08:07,557 --> 02:08:12,657
However, you should wear it to
see how brilliant it is.

940
02:08:13,948 --> 02:08:16,448
I want you to wear this.

941
02:08:17,753 --> 02:08:19,883
If you let me.

942
02:08:20,267 --> 02:08:24,267
You have been with
me for a long time, Feodor.

943
02:08:25,878 --> 02:08:28,968
I always loved tailoring.

944
02:08:33,739 --> 02:08:37,429
This is brilliant.

945
02:08:37,724 --> 02:08:39,954
Very beautiful.

946
02:08:42,565 --> 02:08:44,735
Here it is!

947
02:08:45,566 --> 02:08:51,456
Wait, this part looks.. as if...

948
02:08:53,156 --> 02:08:55,216
no, no...

949
02:08:57,647 --> 02:08:59,637
this part...

950
02:09:00,917 --> 02:09:03,837
this shoulder...

951
02:09:04,706 --> 02:09:08,426
looks bad.

952
02:09:52,296 --> 02:09:54,126
If...

953
02:09:56,915 --> 02:09:59,615
I was not from a noble family...

954
02:10:00,500 --> 02:10:05,260
and I was not a Lord in Bithynia...

955
02:10:08,462 --> 02:10:11,112
I would be a tailor.

956
02:10:13,333 --> 02:10:18,643
However, it can't always happen.

957
02:10:33,907 --> 02:10:36,687
I hope you understand me.

958
02:10:43,061 --> 02:10:47,921
I can't...

959
02:10:54,551 --> 02:10:59,421
Next time...

960
02:10:59,672 --> 02:11:03,232
do what duty I give to you.

961
02:11:05,626 --> 02:11:09,626
Because of your silliness...

962
02:11:12,449 --> 02:11:16,769
we don't know where Father Gregor is.

963
02:11:26,097 --> 02:11:28,977
Mashallah, my son.

964
02:11:33,915 --> 02:11:36,675
I'm so happy for you, Osman Bey.

965
02:11:42,214 --> 02:11:45,074
What, Malhun Hatun?

966
02:11:45,835 --> 02:11:50,725
Bala Hatun is pregnant. My Orhan
will have a sibling.

967
02:11:55,157 --> 02:11:59,537
Thank you.
It's a miracle.

968
02:12:02,015 --> 02:12:04,355
My Allah made Bala happy.

969
02:12:08,749 --> 02:12:12,259
Every pray has an answer.

970
02:12:17,998 --> 02:12:20,438
Come here.

971
02:12:21,710 --> 02:12:24,740
I want to talk to you about it.

972
02:12:39,461 --> 02:12:42,571
You have come to me.

973
02:12:43,100 --> 02:12:45,790
We have our Orhan now.

974
02:12:46,770 --> 02:12:48,950
You have become my Hatun.

975
02:12:49,658 --> 02:12:51,838
You have become my comrade.

976
02:12:54,134 --> 02:12:57,034
You will always be important to me.

977
02:13:06,736 --> 02:13:10,736
Don't be sad.

978
02:13:12,018 --> 02:13:17,408
I know it's hard.

979
02:13:21,221 --> 02:13:23,581
Don't worry...

980
02:13:25,884 --> 02:13:31,124
my Allah will make you
happy with our Orhan.

981
02:13:46,501 --> 02:13:52,171
Thank you, my Bey.

982
02:13:52,564 --> 02:13:54,664
You have cured my troubles.

983
02:14:06,087 --> 02:14:07,897
My Orhan.

984
02:14:16,667 --> 02:14:18,127
They're here.

985
02:15:35,116 --> 02:15:36,606
Boran.

986
02:15:38,872 --> 02:15:40,282
Bey.

987
02:15:43,993 --> 02:15:45,583
What happened?

988
02:15:47,963 --> 02:15:49,683
Who did this?

989
02:15:52,358 --> 02:15:54,548
We dropped Mari and set off.

990
02:15:59,050 --> 02:16:01,260
Then we got ambushed.

991
02:16:07,462 --> 02:16:09,922
Who did this?

992
02:16:11,815 --> 02:16:13,415
Who?

993
02:16:15,168 --> 02:16:16,778
Rogatus.

994
02:16:18,414 --> 02:16:20,304
Rogatus' dog.

995
02:16:20,861 --> 02:16:23,175
Bring Karayel, Göktuğ.

996
02:16:23,175 --> 02:16:24,845
Eyvallah (Okay), my Bey.

997
02:16:41,611 --> 02:16:43,271
We'll take his relics...

998
02:16:45,118 --> 02:16:47,327
to Turgut Bey.

999
02:16:51,972 --> 02:16:53,802
Bury the dead..

1000
02:16:55,313 --> 02:16:57,753
Dig the graves of the traitors.

1001
02:16:58,982 --> 02:17:00,752
Your command, my Bey.

1002
02:17:27,758 --> 02:17:28,938
My Bey.

1003
02:17:35,214 --> 02:17:36,644
Karayel.

1004
02:17:57,509 --> 02:17:59,769
Come on, brothers.

1005
02:18:28,236 --> 02:18:29,956
Karayel.

1006
02:18:38,014 --> 02:18:39,655
Karayel!

1007
02:19:03,422 --> 02:19:12,951
Please contact us for any inquiries
turkision@gmail.com